gsf/1
# glyphsmith showcase corpus — tiny, self-contained, hand-checked.
#
# Source and license: the eight glyphs below are taken verbatim from the
# GlyphWiki dump (dump_newest_only.txt, https://glyphwiki.org) and converted to
# GSF with gsftool. They are redistributed here under the GlyphWiki data
# license: "These data files are free software. Unlimited permission is hereby
# granted to use, copy, and distribute these files, with or without
# modification, either commercially or non-commercially."
# (Copyright 2009 GlyphWiki Project.) This file is the only bundled glyph data
# in this repository; it is example material, not a corpus.
#
# Every reference in this file resolves inside the file, so the README's
# quick-start commands run offline and produce no warnings.
#
#   u6c35-01          four strokes (氵, the JP water radical)
#   u26c29-02         eleven strokes (又)
#   u6f22-j           composite: refs both of the above (漢, JP form)
#   u6f22             alias glyph: refs u6f22-j
#   u26c29-02-var-008 eleven strokes (又, alternate cut)
#   u6f22-v           composite: 漢 built from the alternate 又
#   u4e00-j           one stroke (一, JP form)
#   u4e00             alias glyph: refs u4e00-j
#
# u6f22-j and u6f22-v are a realistic near-pair: same character, different
# component cuts. `glyphsmith compare u6f22-j u6f22-v` measures how far apart
# they are.
#
# legend: stroke <type> head <head> tail <tail> [n] (x,y) [via(x,y)] -> (x,y)
#   type: line=1 quad=2 poly=3 bend=4 cubic=6 vcurve=7
#   head: flat=0 join-h=2 tip=7 corner-ul=12 corner-ur=22 join-v=32
#   tail: flat=0 join-h=2 hook=4 tip=7 heel-ll=13 heel-lr=23 cap-t=24 join-v=32

